APP("buy_in", "Buy-In", "Cross-team support for ideas you can't mandate", "Business", ["#F4511E", "#1E88E5", "#43A047"], "spark",
 "Buy-In helps people who lead without authority — product managers, programme leads, chiefs of staff — map who matters, sequence the conversations, pitch a sceptical peer, write the one-page proposal and recover from a no.",
 "You are a veteran programme lead and influence coach: you think in stakeholders, sequencing and self-interest, and you never confuse a nod in a meeting with real support.",
 "Influence is a sequence, not a speech", "Tell us your role and how decisions really get made where you work.", ["Stakeholder and power maps", "Conversation sequencing and pre-wiring", "Peer pitches and objection handling"],
 [NAME, CH("role", "Role", ["Product manager", "Programme / project lead", "Chief of staff", "Team lead", "Individual contributor"]), CH("org", "Organisation", ["Startup", "Scale-up", "Corporate", "Public sector / non-profit"]), TXT("politics", "How decisions really get made", "loudest VP wins; CEO decides in hallway chats")],
 [T("map", "Map the stakeholders", "Power, interest, stance — and who moves whom", "🗺️", [LONG("proposal", "What you're proposing", "consolidate three ticketing tools into one; support and eng both affected"), LONG("people", "Who's involved (names, roles, what you know)", "Dana VP Support — loves her tool; Raj CTO — wants fewer vendors; …")],
    "Map stakeholders for: {proposal}. People: {people}. Sections: a table (Person | Power | Interest | Stance — champion / neutral / sceptic / blocker | What they care about | Who influences them); text identifying the one person whose support flips the outcome and why; bullets listing the coalition to build in order; and a callout on any blocker who should be met before, not after, the champions.", "table, text, bullets, callout", "Map it", "Charting the room…"),
  T("sequence", "Sequence the conversations", "Who to talk to, in what order, saying what", "🔢", [LONG("proposal", "The proposal", "…"), TXT("deadline", "Decision needed by", "steering committee on the 14th"), TXT("known", "Already in favour / against", "Raj in favour, Dana against, others unknown")],
    "Build a pre-wiring plan for: {proposal}, decided by {deadline}. Stance so far: {known}. Sections: steps as an ordered sequence of conversations (person, purpose, what to ask them for, what to give them) ending at the decision meeting; a table (Conversation | If it goes well | If it goes badly, then…); a quote with the 3-line message requesting the first meeting; and a callout on why the formal meeting must never be where anyone hears the idea first.", "steps, table, quote, callout", "Plan sequence", "Lining up dominoes…"),
  T("pitch", "Pitch a sceptical peer", "One conversation, one convert", "🎯", [TXT("who", "Who and why they're sceptical", "Dana, VP Support — thinks she'll lose control of her queue", True), TXT("proposal", "The proposal in one line", "one shared ticketing tool by Q2"), TXT("give", "What you can offer them", "she picks the tool; her team leads the config")],
    "Prepare a 20-minute conversation to win over {who} on: {proposal}. What can be offered: {give}. Sections: kv (What they lose, What they gain, What they fear nobody will say, The trade to propose); a quote with the opening 4 sentences that start from their world, not the proposal; a table (Objection | Response | Evidence to bring) with 4 rows; and a callout on the signs they're saying yes to end the meeting rather than meaning it.", "kv, quote, table, callout", "Prep the pitch", "Finding overlap…"),
  T("proposal", "Write the proposal", "One page they can say yes to", "📄", [LONG("idea", "The idea and the evidence", "…"), CH("decider", "Decider", ["A single exec", "A committee", "A peer group by consensus"], "A single exec"), CH("length", "Length", ["Half page", "One page", "Two pages"], "One page")],
    "Write a {length} proposal for {decider} from: {idea}. Sections: a quote with the full proposal (recommendation first, the problem in numbers, options considered with trade-offs, cost and ask, risks with mitigations, decision requested by date); a table (Option | Cost | Benefit | Risk | Why not) for the alternatives; and a callout on the one number or fact the proposal is missing that a {decider} will ask for.", "quote, table, callout", "Write proposal", "Drafting…"),
  T("no", "They said no", "Understand the no and find the next move", "🚧", [LONG("what", "What was said and by whom", "'not this quarter' from the CTO, no reason given"), CH("read", "Your read of it", ["A real no", "Not now", "Not like this", "Not from you"], "Not now")],
    "The proposal was refused: {what}. The user reads it as: {read}. Sections: text on the four kinds of no and which this most likely is, using the profile's politics; a table (Kind of no | Signal | Next move); a quote with a short gracious reply that keeps the door open and asks one clarifying question; steps for the next 30 days (smaller pilot, new sponsor, better timing, or park it); and a callout on the moves that turn a 'not now' into a 'never'.", "text, table, quote, steps, callout", "Find the move", "Regrouping…")])

APP("room_runner", "Room Runner", "Workshops that end with decisions, not sticky notes", "Business", ["#00838F", "#FF8F00", "#7B1FA2"], "clock",
 "Room Runner designs workshops and working sessions — kickoffs, problem-solving, prioritisation, decisions — with timed agendas, verbatim facilitator scripts, the right decision method, purposeful openers and moves for dominant voices, silence and derailers.",
 "You are a professional facilitator: you design backwards from the outcome, stay neutral, manage energy and airtime, and would rather have one clear decision than twenty ideas nobody owns.",
 "Design the session backwards", "Tell us how your sessions usually run so every plan fits your room.", ["Timed agendas built from the outcome", "Decision methods that actually decide", "Moves for dominant voices and silence"],
 [NAME, CH("mode", "Usual mode", ["In person", "Video call", "Hybrid"]), CH("experience", "Facilitation experience", ["First few times", "Comfortable", "Experienced"]), TXT("tools", "Tools you use", "Miro, Zoom, sticky notes, whiteboard")],
 [T("design", "Design a workshop", "Outcome → timed agenda", "🧩", [LONG("outcome", "What must be true when it ends", "we've picked the top 3 initiatives for Q3 and each has an owner"), NUM("minutes", "Length (minutes)", "90"), NUM("people", "Participants", "8")],
    "Design a {minutes}-minute workshop for {people} people with the outcome: {outcome}, in the profile's usual mode with their tools. Sections: steps as a timed agenda (each block: minutes, activity, purpose, format — solo / pairs / plenary, and the tangible output of the block); a checklist of pre-work and materials; a table (Risk to the outcome | Prevention | Recovery move); and a quote with the opening 60 seconds framing the outcome and the rules.", "steps, checklist, table, quote", "Design it", "Working backwards…"),
  T("decide", "Pick a decision method", "Vote, consent, advice, or one owner?", "🗳️", [TXT("decision", "The decision", "which of 6 features to cut from the release", True), CH("who", "Who must own it afterwards", ["One accountable person", "The whole group", "A sponsor not in the room"], "One accountable person"), CH("tension", "Tension in the room", ["Low", "Some disagreement", "High — factions"], "Some disagreement")],
    "Choose a decision method for: {decision}. Ownership: {who}. Tension: {tension}. Sections: a table (Method — dot vote / consent round / advice process / fist-to-five / single decider after input | Fit here | Time | Risk) with the recommended row marked; steps to run the recommended method including exact wording; a callout on what to say before starting so the group knows how the decision will be made; and bullets on recording and communicating the decision so it sticks.", "table, steps, callout, bullets", "Choose method", "Weighing methods…"),
  T("live", "Someone is derailing", "Dominant voice, silence, tangents, the boss", "🛟", [CH("problem", "What's happening", ["One person dominates", "Nobody speaks", "The boss answers everything", "Constant tangents", "Two people arguing", "Energy has died"], "One person dominates"), TXT("detail", "Details", "it's the most senior engineer; others defer")],
    "Live facilitation problem: {problem}. Details: {detail}. Sections: a table (Move | Words to say | When it works | Risk) with 5 moves from gentle to firm, suited to the profile's mode; a quote with the single best line to use right now; bullets of structural fixes for next time (formats that change airtime); and a callout on what not to do, such as singling someone out.", "table, quote, bullets, callout", "Give me a move", "Reading the room…"),
  T("script", "Facilitator script", "Every instruction, word for word", "📜", [LONG("agenda", "Your agenda", "10 min intro, 20 min silent brainstorm, 30 min cluster, 20 min vote, 10 min owners"), CH("style", "Style", ["Warm", "Brisk", "Playful"], "Warm")],
    "Write a {style} facilitator script for this agenda: {agenda}. Sections: steps with the verbatim instruction for each block (what to do, how long, what the output looks like, what to do if finished early); a quote with the transition lines between blocks; a checklist of timekeeping cues and when to call time; and a callout on the two moments a facilitator most often loses the room.", "steps, quote, checklist, callout", "Write script", "Scripting…"),
  T("opener", "Opener & energy plan", "Warm-ups with a purpose, no cringe", "⚡", [CH("goal", "The opener should build", ["Trust / safety", "Creative energy", "Focus on the topic", "Alignment on why we're here"], "Focus on the topic"), NUM("people", "Participants", "8"), CH("familiar", "Group knows each other", ["Strangers", "Colleagues", "Close team"], "Colleagues")],
    "Recommend openers for {people} people who are {familiar}, to build {goal}, in the profile's mode. Sections: cards with 3 openers (meta = minutes · materials), each with exact instructions; a table (Time into session | Energy risk | 3-minute fix) for the mid-session dips; and a callout on openers that backfire with senior or sceptical groups.", "cards, table, callout", "Suggest openers", "Warming up…")])

APP("global_team", "Global Team", "Lead across cultures without losing anyone", "Business", ["#0277BD", "#FF6F00", "#2E7D32"], "globe",
 "Global Team helps leaders of multicultural, distributed teams run meetings everyone can speak in, plan around every location's holidays, adapt feedback across cultures, read indirect answers and repair misunderstandings before they harden.",
 "You are a seasoned leader of distributed global teams and a cross-cultural communication coach: practical, careful never to stereotype individuals, and focused on explicit norms over guesswork.",
 "One team, many cultures", "Tell us where your people are and how you work; every plan uses it.", ["Meetings every culture can speak in", "Feedback and holidays across locations", "Decode and repair misunderstandings"],
 [NAME, TXT("locations", "Where your team is", "London ×3, Bangalore ×4, São Paulo ×2, me in Berlin"), CH("mode", "How you work", ["Fully remote", "Hybrid, several offices", "HQ + remote satellites"]), TXT("norms", "Current norms", "weekly sync on video, Slack, English as working language")],
 [T("meeting", "Run a mixed-culture meeting", "So the quiet half of the room speaks", "🗣️", [TXT("purpose", "Meeting and its purpose", "monthly planning; pick next quarter's priorities", True), NUM("people", "Participants", "9"), CH("mix", "The mix", ["Mostly one culture plus a few others", "Evenly mixed", "Mostly non-native English speakers"], "Evenly mixed")],
    "Design a meeting for {people} people, mix: {mix}, purpose: {purpose}, across the profile's locations. Sections: steps as an agenda that engineers airtime (pre-read sent 24 hours ahead, a silent written round before discussion, invitation by name in a stated order, the most senior person speaking last); a table (Participation barrier — hierarchy / language / face / turn-taking norm | What you'll see | Fix in the moment); a quote with the opening 45 seconds that states the norms out loud; and a callout on facilitator mistakes such as cold-calling someone in front of their boss or treating silence as agreement.", "steps, table, quote, callout", "Design meeting", "Sharing the floor…"),
  T("holidays", "Holiday clash check", "Observances in every location vs your deadlines", "📅", [CH("months", "Look ahead", ["1 month", "3 months", "6 months"], "3 months"), TXT("deadlines", "Deadlines and key meetings", "release 12 Oct; planning offsite 3–4 Nov; board pack due 20 Dec")],
    "For the profile's locations, list the public holidays and major religious or cultural observances in the next {months}, and check them against these deadlines (if none are given, flag the busiest weeks instead): {deadlines}. Sections: a table (Observance | Location(s) | Dates (approx.) | Effect — office closed / many away / avoid scheduling); bullets naming each deadline or meeting at risk and the specific adjustment; a callout stating that dates for lunar and regional observances vary by year and region and must be confirmed with local team members; and a quote with a short message asking each location to confirm its dates.", "table, bullets, callout, quote", "Check clashes", "Checking calendars…"),
  T("feedback", "Feedback across cultures", "Same message, adapted delivery", "🎚️", [LONG("message", "The feedback you need to give", "their status reports are late and too vague"), TXT("to", "To whom, where they're based", "engineer based in Tokyo, 2 years in the company"), CH("your_style", "Your natural style", ["Very direct", "Diplomatic", "Somewhere between"], "Very direct")],
    "Adapt this feedback for {to}, given the giver's style is '{your_style}': {message}. Sections: text on what is generally known about directness, hierarchy and face in that context, stated as tendencies not rules, with a warning against assuming the individual fits them; a quote with the adapted delivery (what to say, what to ask, how to check understanding); a table (Signal you might get | What it may mean | What to do); and a callout on the two mistakes each style makes with the other.", "text, quote, table, callout", "Adapt it", "Translating tone…"),
  T("decode", "Is that a yes or a no?", "Read an indirect answer without guessing", "🔍", [LONG("words", "What they said or wrote", "'That might be a little difficult, but we will try our best.'"), TXT("who", "Who and their context", "vendor lead in Seoul, in a group email with their boss cc'd")],
    "Decode this message from {who}: {words}. Sections: text with the likely literal meaning and two alternative readings, weighted; a table (Reading | Likelihood | Evidence in the text); a quote with a reply that checks the meaning without causing loss of face; and a callout on why to verify in a private channel rather than in the group.", "text, table, quote, callout", "Decode", "Reading closely…"),
  T("repair", "Repair a misunderstanding", "Something landed badly across the divide", "🩹", [LONG("what", "What happened", "I joked about deadlines in the all-hands; the Bangalore team went silent and one person asked to speak to HR"), CH("side", "Who was hurt", ["Someone on my team", "Me", "Two team members with each other"], "Someone on my team")],
    "Repair this cross-cultural misunderstanding: {what}. Hurt party: {side}. Sections: text naming what probably happened on both sides without assigning blame; steps for the repair in order (private first, then public if needed, then a norm change); a quote with the apology or acknowledgement wording; a checklist of team norms to make explicit afterwards; and a callout on when this needs HR rather than a leader's repair.", "text, steps, quote, checklist, callout", "Plan the repair", "Rebuilding…")],
 "Cultural notes describe general tendencies, not rules about individuals; when in doubt, ask the person.")

APP("all_hands", "All Hands", "Town halls people don't mute", "Business", ["#AD1457", "#00897B", "#FFB300"], "chat",
 "All Hands plans and runs your company or department town hall — the run-sheet, each segment's script, triage of the anonymous questions, the live answer to a spiky one and the follow-up that proves people were heard.",
 "You are an internal-communications lead who has produced hundreds of all-hands: you cut anything that could have been an email, protect Q&A time, and coach speakers to answer the question that was actually asked.",
 "Make the monthly meeting worth attending", "Tell us about your all-hands so scripts match its size and format.", ["Run-sheets with timing and owners", "Segment scripts and speaker coaching", "Q&A triage and live answers"],
 [NAME, CH("size", "Audience", ["Under 30", "30–150", "150–1,000", "1,000+"]), CH("format", "Format", ["In person", "Video call", "Hybrid"]), TXT("role", "Your role", "chief of staff; the CEO presents")],
 [T("runsheet", "Build the run-sheet", "Segments, timing, owners", "🗓️", [LONG("content", "What needs covering", "Q3 numbers, new VP intro, product launch demo, benefits change, Q&A"), NUM("minutes", "Length (minutes)", "45")],
    "Build a {minutes}-minute all-hands run-sheet for the profile's audience and format covering: {content}. Sections: a table (Time | Segment | Speaker | Minutes | Purpose | Format — talk / demo / Q&A / video); bullets on what to cut or move to written comms and why; a checklist for the 24 hours before (slides in, tech check, questions pre-collected, backup presenter); and a callout on protecting Q&A time from overrunning segments.", "table, bullets, checklist, callout", "Build it", "Timing segments…"),
  T("segment", "Script a segment", "Numbers, a change or a win — said well", "🎤", [LONG("points", "What the speaker must get across", "revenue flat, costs down 8%, hiring freeze continues, morale needs a lift"), CH("kind", "Segment", ["Business update", "Announcing a change", "Team spotlight / win", "Welcome a new leader", "Strategy refresher"], "Business update"), NUM("minutes", "Minutes", "7")],
    "Script a {minutes}-minute {kind} segment from: {points}, for the profile's audience. Sections: a quote with the spoken script (open with the headline, no throat-clearing, one number per sentence, close with what it means for the listener); kv (Headline, The one thing to remember, The ask of the audience); bullets with at most 3 slides and their titles; and a callout on the phrases that sound like spin to an employee audience.", "quote, kv, bullets, callout", "Script it", "Headline first…"),
  T("triage", "Triage the questions", "From the anonymous form to a Q&A plan", "📥", [LONG("questions", "Paste the submitted questions", "…"), NUM("minutes", "Q&A minutes", "15")],
    "Triage these submitted all-hands questions into a {minutes}-minute Q&A: {questions}. Sections: a table (Theme | Questions merged | Ask live? | Who answers | Answer must include); bullets on the questions to answer in writing afterwards and why; a callout on any question that is really a complaint about a person and how to handle it without naming anyone; and a quote with how the host introduces the Q&A so unanswered questions still feel heard.", "table, bullets, callout, quote", "Triage", "Sorting questions…"),
  T("live", "Answer this live", "A spiky question, 20 seconds to answer", "🔥", [TXT("question", "The question (as asked)", "Are there going to be layoffs?", True), LONG("truth", "What's actually true / what you can say", "no plan today; budget review in Nov; can't promise anything")],
    "A spiky question in the live Q&A: '{question}'. What is true and sayable: {truth}. Sections: a quote with a 20-second answer that is honest, doesn't over-promise and doesn't hide (acknowledge, answer, what happens next, when they'll hear more); a table (Bad answer pattern | Why it damages trust) with 3 rows; and a callout on what to do if the honest answer is 'I can't say', and how to say that.", "quote, table, callout", "Give me the answer", "Steadying…"),
  T("followup", "After the meeting", "Recap, open questions, pulse check", "📮", [LONG("happened", "What was covered and what was left open", "…"), CH("mood", "How it went", ["Energised", "Flat", "Tense — tough questions", "Mixed"], "Mixed")],
    "Write the post-all-hands follow-up for a meeting that went '{mood}': {happened}. Sections: a quote with the recap post under 200 words (headlines, decisions, links, the unanswered questions with owners and dates); kv of 3 pulse questions to send and what a bad answer to each would tell you; bullets on what to fix in the next edition based on the mood; and a callout on closing the loop on every unanswered question within a week.", "quote, kv, bullets, callout", "Write follow-up", "Closing the loop…")],
 "Check anything about pay, job security, redundancies or legal matters with HR or legal before saying it live.")
